<title>USA: FSA qualifies 14 issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>FSA qualifies 14 issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Tuesday it qualified for bond insurance the following 14 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Pomona USD, Calif., $10 million GOs.</p>
<p>--San Leandro USD, Calif., $15.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--St. Paul ISD, Minn., $16 million COPs and $11 million school building GOs.</p>
<p>--Caldwell County, N.C., $3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Bound Brook BOE, N.J., $3.93 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Essex County, N.J., $1.718 million college bonds.</p>
<p>--Tarrytown UFSD, N.Y., school district.</p>
<p>--Arlington, Texas, $6.9 million combination purpose and $33.99 million improvement .</p>
<p>--Tacoma, Wash., $29.78 million limited tax GOs and $3 million GO and refunding (tax).</p>
<p>--Sparta, Wis., $1.355 million mortgage revs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
